From 6aad40c3a12b4dbed03ebc9c2632352193b3c5d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bazyli Klockiewicz <bklockiewicz@tenstorrent.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:53:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Kimi K3 reload ring: KV migration from prefill

The ring's HandOff now writes K3's KV chunk table: MLA kvpe "0", KDA S "1" and conv "2".

- The K3 decoder harnesses (sparse KDA, dense KDA, MLA) declare "kv_migration" pins, the same
  kda_transients / mla_transients dicts the spec's hooks read in the regular pipeline, so
  ReloadPipeline records each layer's caches at capture.
- reload_launch: drop the "no KV migration" contract and describe what the table carries; the KDA
  version count is TT_K3_KDA_STATE_SLOTS, not a fixed eight.
- tests/blaze/infra/test_reload_k3_kv_table.py: HandOff's export over three ranks (one with no
  layer) at one and at eight KDA state slots, every layer's rows on its own chips at its own base up
  to its config's extent; mismatched version counts and too few KDA users fail every rank; from_env
  takes K3's hooks; the harnesses declare their pins. Replaces test_hand_off_refuses_a_kv_table_for_k3.
- adding-kv-migration.md: K3's pins and launcher.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
